			<item>
				<title>[AWS Cloud Fundamental Notes] IAM</title>
				<link>https://tech.ray247k.com/en/blog/202301-aws-fundamental-iam/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 10 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://tech.ray247k.com/en/blog/202301-aws-fundamental-iam/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Due to the excessive power of root permissions, it is necessary to divide them into multiple users and groups to set permissions.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://aws.amazon.com/tw/iam/&#34;&#xD;&#xA;   &#xD;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;AWS IAM&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/zh_tw/IAM/latest/UserGuide/introduction.html&#34;&#xD;&#xA;   &#xD;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;What is IAM?&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://i.imgur.com/OtEOMd4.png&#34; alt=&#34;IAM Architecture&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;operation-mechanism&#34;&gt;Operation Mechanism&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The architecture of IAM is as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre class=&#34;mermaid&#34;&gt;graph LR;&#xA;&#xA;Policy1--&gt;Permission;&#xA;Policy2--&gt;Permission;&#xA;Policy3--&gt;Permission;&#xA;Permission--&gt;Role;&#xA;Permission--&gt;Group;&#xA;Group--&gt;User;&#xA;User--&gt;Password;&#xA;User--&gt;Credentail;&#xA;Role--&gt;id1[External Users];&#xA;Role--&gt;id2[AWS Internal Services];&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;policy&#34;&gt;Policy&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/zh_tw/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/iam-policy-structure.html&#34;&#xD;&#xA;   &#xD;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;Official Documentation&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When a policy is attached to a user or group, it allows or denies permission for the user to perform specific tasks on specific resources.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
